the united nations has sounded the alarm  bell on the issue of world refugees it  says the number has exceeded 100 million  for the first time on record in the  words of the unhcr commissioner felipe  granty the figure is sobering and  alarming in equal measure  since the war broke out in february the  rate of refugees and displaced people  has been accelerated as early as march  2.5 million ukrainians left their  country  the u.n is expecting the figure to  exceed 8 million by the end of this year  grandi says the new crisis should not  distract us from the old ones  i think an important message and you  mentioned it joseph is that  there is not just ukraine that we should  not forget all the rest  first of all because ukraine has an  impact on many other  fragile situations making it more fraud  making them more fragile food security  energy crisis  price increases instability  and then this  in turn can cause more displacement  by the end of last june the number of  forcibly displaced people worldwide rose  toward 90 million it's the result of  violence in ethiopia for a faso myanmar  nigeria afghanistan the democratic  republic of the congo and other  countries  as the number of refugees across the  world increases relief agencies become  less capable of handling the situation  the u.n humanitarian office ocha warns  nearly 18 million people are going to  face severe food shortages in the next  three months across the african sahara  region  the office's appeal for 3.8 billion  dollars for relief has generated less  than 12 percent of that amount so far  in palestine  one of the oldest refugee crises goes on  with no end in sight  other refugee crises have been around  for decades as well  governments and international  organizations will now need to think of  a new way to address this unending  problem muhammad al jazeera
 

